  "rendered": "1. Pretreatment of the NiTi wire: aging at 600 °C[1] for 1 h[2] under vacuum, in a tube furnace, before polishing and coating. This aging was used to activate the superelastic/shape-memory property of the alloy.\n2. Vanadium oxide ALD onto the aged wire: the process ran at a reaction temperature of 200 °C[3], with the precursor preheated to 55[4] °C and the manifolds heated to 115[5] °C, and the wires subjected to repeated ALD cycles. This is a deposition step rather than a timed heat treatment, and no separate time is given for it.\n3. Post-deposition anneal of the coating: 450 °C[6] for 30 min[7] in a tube furnace open to air, to crystallize the coating into V2O5.[8][9]",
